# CRUD controller design

## Plugin semantics

Controllers load the Crud component, enable actions, and return `$this->Crud->execute()` for CRUD-handled actions. Business customization prefers config and listeners over fat action methods.

## Required behavior

- Follow the project's existing Crud component / listener registration patterns.
- Keep controller actions thin when CRUD executes them.
- Place reusable lifecycle behavior in listeners (see listeners rule) unless `.ai/` says otherwise.

## Preferred patterns

- Enable only needed actions.
- Configure action settings in controller `initialize` / Crud config consistent with the app.
- Delegate substantial `Crud.*` handling to dedicated listener classes.

## Anti-patterns

- Large action methods that duplicate Crud execute flow
- Anonymous closures for substantial reusable lifecycle logic
- Persistence rules implemented only in the controller
